    '**HANDOVER · chief accountant · N. Antoun · for my successor · 25 September · six pages',
    '**HOW THIS IS ORGANISED, AND WHY.** **By decision, in the order the decisions will arrive, not by file. The handover I received was fourteen pages organised by file; I found every file within a week and it took me nine months to learn what to do with them. The file list is two lines at the end.**',
    '**DECISION 1 · THE PAYMENT RUN, FIRST THURSDAY, IN FOUR DAYS.** **What is decided: which invoices are paid and which wait. Who decides: you, up to 500,000, and two signatures above it with no exception not authorised in advance. What it rests on: the aged supplier list and the cash forecast.** **The last three times: in July I paid Qasioun in full and held Anadolu for a proforma; in August I part-paid a disputed invoice at 765,000 and told the supplier beforehand; in September I refused a verbal request from a director for 240,000 in cash and wrote the refusal down. Who will know if it goes wrong: the supplier, before we do.**',
    '**DECISION 2 · THE CLOSE, FIFTH WORKING DAY.** **What is decided: what is estimated and what waits for evidence. What it rests on: the stock count sheets and the four bank reconciliations.** **The last three times: in June I took work in progress as an estimate and said so above the figure; in July I held the close a day for the Latakia sheets and told Dubai before the pack; in August I closed with the bank confirmation outstanding and wrote it in "what did not happen".**',
