  wModel: { title: 'an application', lines: [
    '**APPLICATION · financial controller · N. Antoun · 25 September · two pages',
    '**THREE THINGS I DECIDED, WITH WHAT FOLLOWED.** **The written standard on payment authorisation, in force 1 July, with its exception, its record and its consequence: eight breaches in August and September last year became two in the three months after it. The claim against Qasioun in April, which put the clause, the invoice and the figure in its first four lines and produced 135,000 in nine days after three earlier letters had been ignored for eleven weeks. The risk note of 24 June, which put a 2 million single-signature exposure in writing for the first time, with three actions that cost a letter, a sentence and a line in a book.**',
    '**ONE THING I GOT WRONG, WITH WHAT FOLLOWED.** **In June I wrote that the Adra plant was being run inefficiently. Nothing in the eleven points of variance supported it, the plant manager read it before the director did and telephoned, and I withdrew it. Every variance note in this pack now carries a line on what the figure does not show, because of that.**',
    '**WHY THAT PARAGRAPH IS ON THIS PAGE.** **Because a page of nothing but successes is read as a page of selections, and the panel knows that nobody has four good years without a bad month. An error with nothing after it is a confession; an error with a change after it is a record.**',
    '**ONE THING I CANNOT YET DO.** **Prepare a group reporting pack to a timetable set outside this company. Three months — two cycles and a quarter end — with somebody beside me for the first two packs. Nobody internal has done it, so the choice before the panel is between a candidate who knows that and one who does not.**',
    '**WHAT I AM ASKING FOR, EXACTLY.** **The financial controller’s post, with those three months written into the appointment letter, and two named days of the group reporting manager’s time in the first month — named days, because "some help" from a thousand miles away becomes an email in August.**',
    '**AND IF THE PANEL APPOINTS SOMEBODY ELSE.** **Three months preparing the group pack alongside whoever is appointed, from the May close to the July quarter end: an hour or two of their time a month, and it leaves this company with two people who can produce the pack, which it does not have today.** **Nothing in these two pages mentions the other candidate, and nothing says I would be well suited to anything.**' ] },
